window.GWENT_EXTRA = {"1123": "I name thee Dea and embrace thee as my daughter.", "1161": "Ugly – nature's way of saying stay away.", "1171": "Me? 'Fraid o' some ploughin' eki-what's-it? Why, it's just an overgrown bat!", "1173": "There are many species of harpy, and all are kleptomaniacs.", "1324": "Stone fists to stop intruders armed with swords. Ironclad logic to stop those armed with lies.", "1325": "That a bird? That a griffin? Naye! That's a…", "1498": "A member of the Bovine Defense Force. Semper fi!", "1516": "Tall one's Wilmar. Wilfred's to his right. And the lad with the stutter's Wilhelm.", "1513": "In Beauclair, everything is better: the wine is sweeter, the cows are bigger and all the ladies are above average.", "1636": "Shupe is known to have quite the imagination. What other troll would look at holes in the ground and see portals?", "1637": "Shupe is known to have quite the imagination. What other troll would look at sticks and see crossbow bolts?", "1638": "Shupe is known to have quite the imagination. What other troll would look at red cardinals and see wyverns?", "1141": "”What have I done?” the mage cried out, frightened of his own creation.", "1779": "Easy, mates! Sirens never attack when... Huh? What d'yous mean Right above me?", "1506": "Only death can cleanse me o' shame.", "1831": "Gernichora's a little like a vampire, they're kindred creatures. 'Cept instead of feasting on the blood of others, she feeds them her own.", "1832": "One, two, come into view; Three, four, hide 'hind the door; Five, six, this'll be quick; Seven, eight, come meet your fate!", "1776": "I'm tellin' youse. Bears fear us more than we fear them. Well... Normal bears, I mean.", "1380": "This bear taste funny to you?", "1448": "Don't move! He can't see us if we don't move.", "1910": "Great is my faith, and great is my ire!", "1946": "Blech! What is this! That's piss, not beer!", "1969": "In Zerrikania, they’re considered a symbol of resurrection. But to be born again, first you have to die.", "1970": "The witchers thought the Salamandra thugs wouldn't get through Kaer Morhen's walls. The witchers were wrong.", "2045": "I lived in a bottle once, but I prefer Ofiri lamps, they're much more comfortable.", "2046": "I call the tiny one Yersinia. She's cute, isn't she?", "2043": "When among crows, you must caw like they do.", "2186": "If they will not submit, they shall be driven out!", "2187": "After having lived over six hundred and fifty years, little remains to excite.", "2233": "The grit of constant suffering had festered in him an unstoppable thirst for inflicting the same pain onto others.", "1232": "He did not stop until the islands were his and the head of the old jarl lay on the ground before him.", "1357": "His visions both terrified Jacques and made him determined to become stronger.", "2198": "The Grand Master did not hesitate to try anything that could save everything.", "2231": "Anyone can join The Order – a knight, a peasant, even a witcher.", "2218": "He was banished just for being what Belohun couldn’t be anymore: young, vital, and strong.", "2219": "Revenge is a dish that tastes best when served for two.", "2058": "For joining the army you shall receive no greater reward than the glory of the battle itself. And gold. Gold is great too.", "2071": "The general had a great talent for transforming idiotic orders into brilliantly executed maneuvers.", "2072": "There were but two options: wash the blood born of foolish orders or wash the blood of the fool himself. A simple decision really.", "2184": "After the curse was lifted Duny claimed ignorance regarding its origin, or who was responsible. He was lying, of course.", "2056": "The tricky part isn’t getting on the roof. It’s how to get down without killing yourself.", "2206": "The queen wanted to protect that which was most important - Brokilon and its children. However, it’s sometimes impossible to save everyone.", "2207": "After the Battle of the Ribbon, Morénn's body was so massacred that even Silver-Eyed could not recognize her own daughter.", "2061": "She can share her arrows with you, but not her apple.", "2060": "I’m not wandering around, I’m roaming! Can’t you see the difference?", "1721": "And thus she reveals herself, the Fairhaired Lady, adorned in flowers full. All life, both plant and beast, follows closely her step, clinging in earnest to her being.", "1132": "We never hunt in these woods. Not even if it means the whole village'll starve.", "1283": "The summer sun reflected in the quiet waters of the Alba – that's Nilfgaard to me.", "2304": "Four out of ten boys survive… at most.", "1100": "I's a war veteran! Spare me a crown?", "1102": "I's a war veteran! Spare me a crown?", "1535": "In Ysgith, the blood of Gernichora weaves the webs.", "3363": "Expecto pa⁠— No, wait. That’s not right.", "3806": "Cursed, exiled, beset - and all this in one luncheon gown.", "4019": "Seven eternities of really bad luck.", "4032": "The elements have failed to halt Bjorn's search. What good will time do?", "4033": "Like a sunflower, it lives to face the great fire in the sky.", "4073": "Time's fun when you're having flies.", "4087": "Looks can be deceiving.", "1881": "Although her father promised her to the gods to win their favour in battle, Gudrun refused to be bound by vows she didn't make. She found her freedom among blue waters and salty wind.", "4133": "No, you're not hallucinating. And yes, they can see you.", "4171": "Like emperor, like empire: Grandiose, entitled, and hell-bent.", "1364": "His sword, forged in the fires of the deep, worthy of being wielded by a god, could crack the earth like lightning. And yet, only his were the hands capable of such artifice.", "4173": "Every living thing is a child of the Queen of the Fields.", "1129": "That is not dead which can eternal lie, and with strange aeons even death may die.", "4178": "Retreat, heathen! I will not axe you twice."};
